# PURPOSE
# -------
# Copies every parquet object from the raw S3 landing zone into a Databricks
# Unity Catalog Volume so downstream Bronze ingestion can read from the Volume
# using standard Spark file paths rather than s3a:// URIs.
#
# Databricks Free Edition serverless compute does not allow setting
# fs.s3a.access.key at runtime, so we download S3 objects through boto3/Python
# instead of mounting S3 with Spark.
#
# INSTRUCTIONS
# ------------
# 1. Upload this file to your Databricks workspace as a Python notebook.
# 2. Fill in the PLACEHOLDERS below with your AWS credentials.
# 3. Run all cells.  The summary table at the bottom confirms success.
# 4. *** DELETE THIS ENTIRE FILE OR REMOVE THE CREDENTIAL CELL BEFORE SAVING. ***
#
# HOW TO UPLOAD
# -------------
#   Databricks UI → Workspace → Import → select this .py file → as Notebook
#   Source language: Python

# ── Cell 1: install package if running in a fresh cluster ──────────────────────
# Uncomment the line below if retail_demand is not already installed on the cluster.
